      "message": "Here are the numbers. I compared three fills: the current column walk, column + padding (this CL), and the row walk.\n\nSetup: RT speed 11, IntraBC on, 20 key frames per clip, 16 of my screen recordings (1080p to 5K) and the 11 AOM CTC b2_scc clips, 4:2:0 and 4:4:4, 1 and 4 threads. Each number is the mean over clips of the per-clip median of 5 interleaved rounds (3 so far on x86). I timed the 2x2 pass, the CRC passes, the count and the fill separately.\n\nFill time in ms per key frame, 1 thread, 4:2:0:\n\nColumn\tColumn + pad\tRow\nApple M3 Pro, recordings\t8.33\t7.46\t5.06\nApple M3 Pro, CTC\t3.60\t3.34\t2.37\nRyzen 9 5900X (MSVC), recordings\t22.48\t17.54\t14.51\nRyzen 9 5900X (MSVC), CTC\t8.08\t7.93\t6.69\nRow walk against this CL, 1 thread (4 threads for the key frame in brackets), 4:2:0 / 4:4:4:\n\nFill\tHash build\tKey frame\nM3 Pro, recordings\t-31% / -31%\t-13% / -13%\t-2.7% / -2.6% (-2.4% / -2.1%)\nM3 Pro, CTC\t-30% / -30%\t-12% / -12%\t-1.9% / -1.7% (-1.6% / -1.0%)\n5900X, recordings\t-17% / -17%\t-7% / -7%\t-2.0% / -1.4% (-1.7% / -1.5%)\n5900X, CTC\t-18% / -17%\t-7% / -6%\t-1.6% / -1.4% (-1.5% / -0.9%)\n\nThe fill is faster with rows on every clip on both machines. The 2x2, CRC and count stages don\u0027t change, except for a 4% CRC difference on the 5900X.\n\nSize, BD rate over q 6 to 24, row walk against this CL. These runs used plain 218282, and both machines gave the same streams:\n\nRecordings: -0.001% / -0.011% at 1 thread, -0.005% / -0.006% at 4 threads (4:2:0 / 4:4:4).\nCTC: +0.013% / +0.021% at 1 thread, +0.008% / +0.020% at 4 threads.\n\nThe worst clip is Slides2r: +0.12% in 4:2:0 and +0.18% in 4:4:4.\n\nSo the row walk is faster than the padding on both Arm and x86, at a size cost of about 0.02% on average on CTC. I\u0027d like to replace this CL with the row walk if you\u0027re OK with the output change. Or we can leave the column walk as is",
